<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Tuesday through a round of overnight system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The move was in line with the market's expectations.</p>
<p>At 1030 EDT/1430 GMT, the time when the Fed usually intervenes in the market, the federal funds rate was quoted at 5-9/16 percent, slightly above the Fed's 5.50 percent target.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
